| 2 | issue | issue | issue | issue | change | Chinese quotations are present. “吾卒之可以擊” means our troops **can attack**, not “can be struck.” “每戰必殆” states danger, not inevitable death; “一勝一負” supplies no measured coin-flip probability. The third half-victory case includes knowledge of both armies but ignorance of terrain, defeating the gloss “whichever side you know.” The source gives criteria and an authority rule, not the claimed ordered grading algorithm. Overlaps #1. 謀攻 [lines 46–48](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:46), 地形 [lines 131–135](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:131). |
