## Claims elsewhere in the file that the sources contradict

- **Review #4:** “The received text does not say ‘be quick’” overlooks “故兵聞拙速，未睹巧之久也” and “故兵之情主速.” Speed has conditions and costs, but is expressly advocated. 軍爭 is also broader than march speed: it covers deception, signals, morale and attack restrictions. 作戰 [line 21](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:21), 九地 [line 140](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:140), 軍爭 [lines 96–102](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:96).
- **Review #8:** “Every virtue is a lever against you” generalizes five specified dangers into all virtues. The source explicitly calls these five “將之過.” 九變 [line 111](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:111).
- **Review #10:** Uncompleted victory being “worse than a plan that failed” is absent; the passage calls it 凶 without that comparison. 火攻 [line 159](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:159).
- **What the top 10 missed:** “You are protected for it” exceeds “退不避罪,” which says the general does not avoid blame or punishment when retreating. “Morale … is a function of time since the last engagement” introduces an elapsed-time variable absent from 朝／晝／暮. 地形 [line 131](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:131), 軍爭 [line 100](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:100).
- **Near misses:** “非仁義不能用間” misquotes “非仁義不能**使**間”; 用間 belongs to the preceding 聖智 clause. 用間 [line 166](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:166).
- **Gaps:** 答話 is not entirely the listed eight terrain exchanges plus entering 郢, and does not end at the 何氏 note. It continues with dead-ground tactics, attacks against arrogant or entrenched enemies, generalship qualities, 《孫子占》 material and editorial attribution cautions. [Lines 194–204](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:194).
- **Not checkable here:** The claims about 〈吳問〉 belonging to the 曹操 edition, its bamboo title and the cited scholars are unsupported by the supplied files. Likewise, these files cannot verify modern historical controversy, the author’s fetching process, or collation against older witnesses.

## Missing

- **Human intelligence as the basis of foreknowledge:** “先知者 … 必取於人，知敵之情者也,” followed by five spy types and the central role of recruited enemy spies. Observation in #11 does not cover this sourcing rule or intelligence system. 用間 [lines 162–168](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:162).
- **Adaptation without a fixed winning form:** “兵無成勢，無恒形，能因敵變化而取勝者，謂之神.” This supplies a clearer rule than #5’s promise of an uncopyable victory or #10’s exclusive fixed response. 虛實 [lines 87–89](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:87).
- **Combining ordinary and extraordinary forces:** “以正合，以奇勝” and “奇正相生” describe a distinct combat method omitted from the twelve. 兵勢 [line 64](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:64).
- **Care joined to enforceable discipline:** “卒未親附而罰之，則不服” and “厚而不能使，愛而不能令 … 不可用也.” These qualify #7’s broad instruction to change conditions rather than people. 行軍 [line 124](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:124), 地形 [line 133](/home/smoke01/dev/ancient-games/runs/20261013-four-seats/sources/sun-tzu/孫子兵法.txt:133).

## Overall

**My reading:** All twelve retain a sourced core, but each needs correction because the English adds structure, changes meaning, or overstates what follows; item 12 also contains a corrupted quotation. **My reading:** I performed this comparison against the supplied texts; it establishes local textual support, without independently establishing historical authorship or the ranking. **Not measured:** The effectiveness of these rules as an agent workflow remains untested here.
